WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:09.760
Tauno.

2
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.720
Look at that nut job.

3
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.040
How did he get on national TV?

4
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.680
This is insane.

5
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.600
Tauno, I can't hide it anymore.

6
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.680
Hide what?

7
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.720
Tell me, honey.

8
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:34.880
I...

9
00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.680
We...

10
00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:40.480
I...

11
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.160
Waited so long
for you to agree to adoption.

12
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.920
Honey, I'm sorry it took a while.

13
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:50.880
I couldn't decide,
but things are alright now.

14
00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:52.080
Everything's alright.

15
00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.080
We'll go there on Friday.

16
00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.280
We'll pick a kid from that shelter
and come back home.

17
00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:02.400
This Friday?
- Yes, Friday. I got a text.

18
00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:05.000
It said we should come
and have a look.

19
00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:09.960
We're just going to meet them,
we don't have to decide anything yet.

20
00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:12.360
Everything is fine.

21
00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.480
I won't back out of this decision.
- I see.

22
00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.040
Aksel and I will go hunting first
and then we'll go hunt for a child.

23
00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.880
That's not how you should say it,
but I'm just so happy.

24
00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.600
DIVORCE IN PEACE

25
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:34.760
What would you do if you were
keeping a secret from your husband

26
00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.320
but you couldn't tell him?

27
00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:39.720
You have to but you can't.

28
00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.880
I would write it down.

29
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.920
And I would decide then.

30
00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.480
Find the right time
and then give the letter to him.

31
00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:53.000
That's a great idea.
- It takes the pressure off.

32
00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.000
You'll be able to decide whether
you actually want to tell him.

33
00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.200
You'll read the
letter first by yourself

34
00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:01.680
and then decide what sounds best.

35
00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:03.800
Okay, okay.

36
00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:08.600
Do you and Tauno have secrets?

37
00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:12.720
No, it's just a small thing
that's bothering me.

38
00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.760
Do you want to tell me first?

39
00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:18.320
No-no, I'll write it down
and then decide what I want to do.

40
00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:20.440
Don't worry.

41
00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.960
You two are having
a good time right now.

42
00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:24.640
Yeah...

43
00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.720
Where are...

44
00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:31.920
I need rubber boots.

45
00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.480
Yours are in the cellar.

46
00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.840
They probably have
things growing on them.

47
00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.960
Right, the cellar.

48
00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:44.800
Do you...

49
00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.880
...think it's a good idea for me
to go into the woods with Tauno?

50
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.160
He's been inviting you for 20 years.

51
00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.840
Give him a chance.

52
00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:57.360
What chance?
- You're his best friend.

53
00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:00.160
He wants to share
his biggest passion with you.

54
00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.920
Be a human and
go shed some blood with him.

55
00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:07.720
That's what I was thinking.
The blood, the guns...

56
00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.840
In some thick bush...

57
00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.720
I think it'll only benefit you.

58
00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.400
Fresh air and something manly.

59
00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:15.880
Is that the problem?

60
00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:17.280
What?

61
00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.120
Am I not manly enough for you?

62
00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:25.960
That I'm just a violin teacher,

63
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:29.560
not some machinist or stone crusher
or special forces guy?

64
00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:31.280
What are you talking about?

65
00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:34.120
Being a violin teacher is very manly.

66
00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:38.880
I just meant to say
that I think it will benefit you.

67
00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:42.960
Shooting in the woods
may cure you of your stage fright.

68
00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.240
Sleeping on moss
instead of a soft mattress.

69
00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.960
I can't even imagine what could...

70
00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:51.400
...be worse than
stumbling around thick woods.

71
00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.520
Stumbling around
thick woods with a crazy person.

72
00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.400
Tauno is...

73
00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.960
He is a professional hunter.

74
00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:02.080
He won't shoot you.

75
00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:05.280
I need to start getting ready.
My nerves are all over the place.

76
00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.680
I need to show Valdek
my jewellery sketches.

77
00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.240
Valdek?

78
00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:12.720
Your coursemate?

79
00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:16.240
Your ex?
- What ex? We were just children.

80
00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:19.640
What can I do?
He runs the gallery.

81
00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:22.560
He seemed fine.

82
00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:24.800
Humble.
He has five kids.

83
00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:28.480
You're meeting your ex-boyfriend
while I'm in the woods?

84
00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.160
Yes.

85
00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:34.120
A wonderful reason to go
and have a breather in the woods.

86
00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.840
Don't worry.

87
00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:38.680
I'd rather come hunting with you two.

88
00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.240
Aksel.

89
00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:43.680
Walkie-talkie.

90
00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.840
Guess I have to go.

91
00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.320
Put on your rubber boots and...

92
00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.240
Your...

93
00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.800
best...

94
00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:01.280
friend...

95
00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:08.880
Aksel...

96
00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:31.480
Dear Tauno,

97
00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:34.520
I've been meaning to
tell you for a while.

98
00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.480
I have made a mistake.

99
00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:41.600
A mistake that may become
the best thing in our lives.

100
00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:45.960
I'm pregnant.

101
00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:51.360
And the father of the baby
is your best friend...

102
00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.360
Aksel.

103
00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.000
Honey! Mirjam!

104
00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.480
Mirjam!

105
00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:00.040
Aksel and I are heading off.

106
00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:02.280
Did you take your wool socks?

107
00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:06.280
Yeah, I have everything.
Almost packed the parachute, too.

108
00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:07.800
Give me those forest maps.

109
00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:11.440
I bought them especially for this.
They're more accurate than any GPS.

110
00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:17.760
Aren't you going to wish us luck?

111
00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:21.320
Take care.

112
00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:28.520
Shit.

113
00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.240
Shit, shit, shit!

114
00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:38.080
Well, we used to
do things together with Aksel.

115
00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:39.160
Some...

116
00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:42.720
There were some things.

117
00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:45.800
But that was a long time ago.

118
00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.920
Yeah...
Your schedule doesn't allow for it.

119
00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:52.400
It's not about my schedule.
It has to come from within,

120
00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:55.120
to create and do things together,
and to be together.

121
00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:56.680
What did you do together?

122
00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:58.240
Mutual hobbies?

123
00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:01.640
Who can remember that?
It was a long time ago.

124
00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:05.240
We took dance classes.

125
00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:08.520
You're right.
- That was quite...

126
00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:11.760
Yeah.
- That was a good time.

127
00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:14.840
Twice a week.
Latin dance and waltz.

128
00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:19.960
That's great. And now,
our seventh task, which is...

129
00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.160
'Saying goodbye to a mutual hobby.'

130
00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:26.800
There are couples that have taken
one last clay sculpting class together.

131
00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.840
We did that, too.
- Yeah!

132
00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:35.240
There are couples that have sang
together for one last time,

133
00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:36.960
for example, karaoke.

134
00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:39.920
Went for one last run together.

135
00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:42.560
Photographed trains,
you name it.

136
00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:46.640
On one evening, choose a hobby,

137
00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:49.560
recreate it one last time

138
00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:51.800
and then say goodbye to it.

139
00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:02.640
I didn't know these
rubber boots were so weird.

140
00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:04.720
It's good that they are colourful.

141
00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.840
You'll stand out better.
- What do you mean?

142
00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:11.280
What do you mean? So that
nobody mistakes you for the prey.

143
00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:16.320
Are you ready for an adventure?

144
00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:17.400
Sure.

145
00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:20.640
I promise you
we'll have a great time.

146
00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:22.880
So, we have the cognac,

147
00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:24.880
we have the matches, the oil...

148
00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:29.800
What?

149
00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:32.200
Let's go?

150
00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:33.520
Let's go.

151
00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:35.560
<i>What?</i>

152
00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:38.040
Shit!

153
00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:41.960
I forgot the butchering knife.

154
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.360
I knew I left something behind.
I'll be right back.

155
00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:54.960
I wrote a confession.
- What confession?

156
00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.520
That you got me pregnant.

157
00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:01.200
That we can't adopt because I'm
going to be a mom and you're the dad.

158
00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.560
You wrote...?
- Yes,

159
00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:06.160
because I wanted to know
how it would sound,

160
00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:09.280
and I wanted to hide it,
but then Tauno took it with him.

161
00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:11.040
Where did he put it?
- In the bag.

162
00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:13.120
What bag?
- In his bag.

163
00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:17.840
He took it by accident with the maps.

164
00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:20.560
Shit, shit, shit!

165
00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:22.520
He's coming!

166
00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:26.840
What were you looking for?
- Checking for matches.

167
00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:30.560
This is a proper tool.

168
00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:32.360
It'll even get a
bear's juices flowing.

169
00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:35.040
Let's go.

170
00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:44.880
We'll head off in the morning,
straight from here.

171
00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:47.640
We'll stay the night here.
I know where to go.

172
00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:50.040
I'll take those maps.
- Why?

173
00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:53.400
I'll read the maps
and you'll be the pilot.

174
00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:54.640
The pilot?

175
00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:57.560
You haven't even held a compass.

176
00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:00.600
I'll teach you in the evening.
We'll go over them together.

177
00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:03.960
Let's take our things inside,
we'll stay the night here.

178
00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:06.160
We'll set off early in the morning.

179
00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:08.960
In the evening...

180
00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:11.960
Some guy talk and cognac.

181
00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:13.480
Let's go.

182
00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.200
What a shrub.

183
00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:20.880
A good place to hide a body.
Nobody would find it.

184
00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:22.800
Yeah?
- Yeah.

185
00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:27.520
So...

186
00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:30.840
Be my guest, Aksel.

187
00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:38.920
Laura.
- Hello, Valdek.

188
00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:42.320
Sorry for being a bit late.

189
00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:48.160
So...

190
00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:50.200
You locked the door?

191
00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:52.200
Yes.

192
00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:55.960
We're dealing with delicate issues

193
00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.000
and don't need any distractions.

194
00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:00.120
Delicate issues?

195
00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:02.320
Alright, then.

196
00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:05.320
Let's see if my sketches
are even worth anything.

197
00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:06.320
Laura.

198
00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:10.960
I've been waiting for this moment.

199
00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:13.040
This opportunity.

200
00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:15.160
Opportunity?

201
00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:17.880
Yeah.

202
00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:20.240
You can make up for it now.

203
00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:22.600
What are you talking about?

204
00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:25.440
Suffering all those years...

205
00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:28.120
The inferiority...

206
00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:31.280
I was discarded like a rag.

207
00:12:31.320 --> 00:12:32.840
Stop it, Valdek.

208
00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:34.640
Now it's my turn.

209
00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:36.720
Alright, let me out.

210
00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:38.120
Wait, wait, wait.

211
00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:39.960
We're just looking at the sketches.

212
00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:42.400
Let's see what I think about them.

213
00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.920
Then we can see
how you can change my opinion.

214
00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:48.440
Valdek, this is harassment.

215
00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:50.880
Things won't end well for you
if you don't let me out.

216
00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:51.920
Wait, wait.

217
00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:54.360
You decided to come here.

218
00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:56.840
I didn't invite you.

219
00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:59.320
You came voluntarily.

220
00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:02.920
You came to show off.

221
00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:06.040
A talented jewellery designer.

222
00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:08.080
Well...

223
00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:11.120
Let's have a look, then.

224
00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:13.760
Let's see how talented you are.

225
00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:15.160
Valdek, stop it.

226
00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:16.920
Stop it now!

227
00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:18.240
Valdek, stop messing around.

228
00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:23.040
Hello.
- Hi.

229
00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:29.160
The lock doesn't work...

230
00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:30.720
...sometimes.

231
00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.080
I think that...

232
00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:46.840
I'd have a harder time
dealing with your hobbies.

233
00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:50.560
If you made me play a violin...
No, even to listen to one,

234
00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:53.240
I would hit myself over the head
within five minutes.

235
00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:57.480
But I appreciate what you do.
I really do.

236
00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:00.280
I understand that it's about me.
I'm simple,

237
00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:04.240
but that doesn't mean
that I don't know how to appreciate.

238
00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:07.640
That everything else is shit.

239
00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:11.520
I also don't think that you...

240
00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:14.600
I also appreciate what you do.

241
00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:17.040
You do it with love.

242
00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:21.200
I can see that the forest,
the animals and the guns...

243
00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:24.920
The main thing is
that you do it with love.

244
00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:26.120
That's true.

245
00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:27.760
I kill animals,

246
00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:30.640
but I do it with great love.

247
00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.880
To kill with love

248
00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:35.440
is noble in some ways.

249
00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:40.000
Let's have a look.
There should be a new ambush point.

250
00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:44.640
I don't want to go there,
I have a good old place...

251
00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:48.560
Wait! What does this sign
over here mean?

252
00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:53.320
This is an old sacrificial stone.
A heritage site.

253
00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:57.720
The old folks were said to have done
sacrifices there, even human ones.

254
00:14:58.560 --> 00:15:00.120
So...

255
00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:03.360
Hold on now!

256
00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:06.640
Forgive me, Tauno.

257
00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:12.640
'Forgive me, Tauno.'

258
00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:16.160
Tauno forgives you.

259
00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:29.000
Rihard, hi.

260
00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:31.400
I have a strange question.

261
00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:33.480
What are you doing right now?

262
00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:35.560
Yeah.

263
00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:39.960
I had a meeting
and things turned quite ugly.

264
00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.360
Yeah, I could use some support.

265
00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:48.400
Okay.

266
00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:50.840
Let's meet up.

267
00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.400
Shit, what a maniac.

268
00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:07.520
Come into the nest.
Come on now!

269
00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:10.160
Two-and-a-half hours of sleep
and then we're off.

270
00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:12.640
Have you slept with gloves on before?

271
00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:15.000
Alright.

272
00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:09.560
Shit, shit.

273
00:17:10.600 --> 00:17:11.920
Shit.

274
00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:58.160
We don't have to
drive anywhere, just...

275
00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:00.640
It's great that you could come.

276
00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:03.760
Was it that scary?

277
00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:07.960
Some men just get worse with age.

278
00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:12.760
I'm glad that you called me.

279
00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:17.000
I don't know...

280
00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:20.360
You seem kind of...

281
00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:23.760
Yeah?

282
00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:30.480
Kind of...

283
00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:50.480
Sorry.

284
00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:55.400
No worries.

285
00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:58.240
I'm alive.

286
00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:08.800
Do I take you home?

287
00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:13.800
I'm not in a hurry anywhere.

288
00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:17.640
Me neither.

289
00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:55.080
Why are you panting?

290
00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:56.920
What?
- What were you doing?

291
00:19:56.920 --> 00:19:58.080
Nothing.

292
00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:00.160
Is it time to go?
- Is it?

293
00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:02.200
Let's go, then.

294
00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:14.920
Soon, we'll have to be quieter.

295
00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:18.960
Look, a branch.

296
00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:29.520
Ouch!

297
00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:33.120
What happened?
- Shit!

298
00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:36.320
I sprained my ankle.

299
00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:39.600
Shit.
- We haven't even gone 50 metres.

300
00:20:39.640 --> 00:20:41.320
Let me straighten it.

301
00:20:41.680 --> 00:20:43.240
No, no, no!

302
00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:47.480
My toe is completely backwards.
I need a doctor.

303
00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:51.160
Can you walk?

304
00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:56.080
That bad?
- My toe is backwards.

305
00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:59.360
Let's go back.
- Well let's go then.

306
00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:02.240
Wait.

307
00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:03.880
Go on, now.
- Wait.

308
00:21:10.760 --> 00:21:13.400
Can you manage?
- I can't hold up my leg.

309
00:21:14.360 --> 00:21:16.840
Shit, people throw paper everywhere.

310
00:21:16.840 --> 00:21:18.040
Don't pick it up!

311
00:21:18.080 --> 00:21:19.560
Could've been a bathroom break!

312
00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:22.720
Look! It's brown on the edges.

313
00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:24.680
Who would go there? A bear?

314
00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:28.600
Easy, now, easy.
- Ouch!

315
00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:32.600
What's going on?
- He sprained his ankle.

316
00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:35.880
I thought he stepped into a trap,
but it's just a bent toe.

317
00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:39.840
Did he kill him?

318
00:21:40.680 --> 00:21:41.680
Who?

319
00:21:41.680 --> 00:21:45.760
I tripped over a log
and now my toe is all backwards.

320
00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:48.800
Stay still.

321
00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:53.240
Ouch, ouch, ouch!

322
00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:55.720
I'm just looking.

323
00:21:55.760 --> 00:21:58.360
Mirjam is a yoga instructor.
She knows what she's doing.

324
00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:02.160
Having your toe backwards is no yoga.

325
00:22:05.160 --> 00:22:06.840
What are you doing?

326
00:22:07.360 --> 00:22:10.560
It's destroyed.
Destroyed.

327
00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:16.400
All good.

328
00:22:18.160 --> 00:22:19.160
What?

329
00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:21.480
Is it alright?
- It's alright.

330
00:22:21.600 --> 00:22:23.280
Put your boots on, we're going back.

331
00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:26.120
Stop, stop.
I think that's enough for today.

332
00:22:26.120 --> 00:22:30.080
Yeah, I think we've
had enough for this time.

333
00:22:30.360 --> 00:22:33.040
Feel that unity for one last time.

334
00:22:33.680 --> 00:22:34.680
That trust.

335
00:22:35.600 --> 00:22:37.560
Do something that
connected the two of you.

336
00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:40.080
Whatever that hobby was.

337
00:22:40.600 --> 00:22:44.600
For example, I had a couple
who went skydiving one last time.

338
00:22:45.720 --> 00:22:48.280
It was a rather difficult divorce.

339
00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:52.120
There was a lot of tension, blame,
a horrible asset division,

340
00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:55.240
but they did everything
just like in the good old days.

341
00:22:55.640 --> 00:22:58.680
The woman packed
the man's parachute and vice versa.

342
00:22:58.960 --> 00:22:59.960
Really?

343
00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:02.000
And both landed safe and sound?

344
00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:09.400
What?

345
00:23:11.920 --> 00:23:16.920
What else could we take from
the myriad of hobbies that we had?

346
00:23:17.280 --> 00:23:21.800
All of our hobbies
went down the Niagara Falls.

347
00:23:21.800 --> 00:23:23.840
But you liked clay moulding.

348
00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:25.800
I liked it ever since I was a child.

349
00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:29.280
As soon as I saw mud,
I wanted to mould something out of it.

350
00:23:29.600 --> 00:23:32.080
I had talent.
I could have become

351
00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:34.880
a bowl sculptor.
- Yeah.

352
00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:37.960
Clay or violin,
both require finger work.

353
00:23:38.240 --> 00:23:41.080
Maybe you'd like to dance?
- I don't.

354
00:23:41.080 --> 00:23:43.520
Let's move the furniture
and take some bigger steps.

355
00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:45.640
No, it's too physical.

356
00:23:45.640 --> 00:23:48.440
It's sweaty and your toes are heavy.
No, I don't want to.

357
00:23:48.440 --> 00:23:50.600
So we're sticking to clay?
- Yeah.

358
00:23:50.640 --> 00:23:53.320
I'll do you and you'll do me.

359
00:23:53.840 --> 00:23:55.560
So romantic.

360
00:23:55.560 --> 00:23:58.880
I will kick you
if you make me look fat and ugly.

361
00:23:58.920 --> 00:24:03.080
I'll make you into
Aphrodite in her seashell.

362
00:24:03.520 --> 00:24:06.120
Venus was the one in the seashell.
- Venus, right.

363
00:24:07.960 --> 00:24:09.120
What...?

364
00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:11.640
It's a snake. Sorry!

365
00:24:11.680 --> 00:24:13.080
Let's start again.

366
00:24:13.120 --> 00:24:16.240
Stop playing around.
I can't work like this.

367
00:24:16.280 --> 00:24:18.480
How can I work on my hobby

368
00:24:18.520 --> 00:24:20.960
if I have to be completely still?

369
00:24:23.400 --> 00:24:25.440
It's quite enlightening

370
00:24:25.480 --> 00:24:29.800
when you have to focus so hard
on a person you've gotten so used to.

371
00:24:30.040 --> 00:24:32.240
Yeah, it's like a piece of furniture.

372
00:24:32.640 --> 00:24:34.040
You're so used to them.

373
00:24:34.080 --> 00:24:38.320
But the next moment
you notice some...

374
00:24:39.360 --> 00:24:42.560
...ribbons and buttons.

375
00:24:43.360 --> 00:24:45.160
Some wrinkles...

376
00:24:45.160 --> 00:24:46.840
And some scars...
- Where?

377
00:24:47.080 --> 00:24:48.160
Everywhere.

378
00:24:49.160 --> 00:24:51.240
It's so interesting.
- What?

379
00:24:52.840 --> 00:24:56.960
You can still find something
new underneath those wrinkles.

380
00:25:00.240 --> 00:25:01.880
What can you see there?

381
00:25:05.720 --> 00:25:06.840
Damn...

382
00:25:07.880 --> 00:25:11.560
How can I when my hands...
Shit...

383
00:25:14.080 --> 00:25:15.320
I'll go.

384
00:25:15.360 --> 00:25:17.840
No, no, no.
I'll go.

385
00:25:17.920 --> 00:25:21.560
I'll leave this biosphere
and you can chat away.

386
00:25:23.680 --> 00:25:24.760
Thank you.

387
00:25:30.280 --> 00:25:31.600
How do I...?

388
00:25:38.000 --> 00:25:39.000
Hello, Rihard.

389
00:25:39.040 --> 00:25:40.040
Hello.

390
00:25:42.040 --> 00:25:43.440
Yeah, this is Mihkel.

391
00:25:45.880 --> 00:25:46.920
What?

392
00:25:48.480 --> 00:25:50.240
An interview with me?

393
00:25:51.680 --> 00:25:54.080
No, my parents don't know about this.

394
00:25:55.840 --> 00:25:56.840
Yeah.

395
00:25:56.920 --> 00:25:58.960
Send it to my e-mail.

396
00:25:59.280 --> 00:26:01.160
I'll send you the address.

397
00:26:01.840 --> 00:26:02.840
Okay.

398
00:26:04.120 --> 00:26:05.800
Yeah, thanks.

399
00:26:07.280 --> 00:26:08.280
Well?

400
00:26:09.240 --> 00:26:10.840
It was a journalist.

401
00:26:11.360 --> 00:26:12.640
He wants to do an interview.

402
00:26:13.480 --> 00:26:14.680
That's so cool.

403
00:26:14.960 --> 00:26:16.200
Your fame is rising.

404
00:26:16.600 --> 00:26:18.760
Shit, this is bad.

405
00:26:26.400 --> 00:26:28.080
Tauno.

406
00:26:28.120 --> 00:26:30.000
Tauno, I can't.

407
00:26:31.800 --> 00:26:34.520
Everything's fine.
We'll go tomorrow morning at 11.

408
00:26:34.720 --> 00:26:36.240
Everything's been agreed on.

409
00:26:36.240 --> 00:26:39.600
The adoption process may begin.

410
00:26:39.640 --> 00:26:41.080
It's not that.

411
00:26:41.120 --> 00:26:43.080
Tauno, I can't anymore.

412
00:26:44.080 --> 00:26:45.080
What's up?

413
00:26:47.240 --> 00:26:49.560
I can't...
- Did you change your mind?

414
00:26:51.080 --> 00:26:53.120
I can't lie to you anymore.

415
00:26:54.120 --> 00:26:55.360
Lie?

416
00:26:59.120 --> 00:27:02.880
Promise me you'll stay calm, okay?

417
00:27:03.000 --> 00:27:06.480
Whatever it is,
promise me you'll stay calm.

418
00:27:06.520 --> 00:27:07.720
Very calm.

419
00:27:07.760 --> 00:27:09.720
Alright, I promise to stay calm.

420
00:27:15.120 --> 00:27:18.240
I ordered that massage
chair that you didn't want.

421
00:27:19.080 --> 00:27:21.960
God, I thought it was something bad.

422
00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:23.400
What chair? That's fine.

423
00:27:23.400 --> 00:27:25.520
I'm also a little bit pregnant.
- What?

424
00:27:26.560 --> 00:27:27.880
I'm pregnant.

425
00:27:30.040 --> 00:27:32.200
You mean adopting?

426
00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:36.680
No, I'm actually pregnant.
There's a child in my stomach.

427
00:27:38.600 --> 00:27:40.920
Did you use a donor?
- Yeah.

428
00:27:40.960 --> 00:27:43.880
Yeah, I used a donor.

429
00:27:43.880 --> 00:27:46.320
Mirjam.
- I used Aksel.

430
00:27:48.000 --> 00:27:51.240
The donor is called Aksel?
- His name is Aksel.

431
00:27:51.280 --> 00:27:53.640
He is Aksel.

432
00:27:53.640 --> 00:27:55.160
I don't understand.

433
00:27:55.920 --> 00:27:57.520
His name is Aksel.

434
00:27:57.920 --> 00:27:59.400
And he is also...

435
00:28:00.560 --> 00:28:02.320
I'm pregnant with Aksel's child.

436
00:28:02.360 --> 00:28:03.920
It's your Aksel's child.

437
00:28:03.960 --> 00:28:05.080
My Aksel's?

438
00:28:05.640 --> 00:28:08.840
Our Aksel's child? Laura's Aksel?

439
00:28:12.560 --> 00:28:14.840
It was that therapy task.

440
00:28:14.880 --> 00:28:18.680
It went a little out of hand...

441
00:28:19.400 --> 00:28:21.640
One thing led to another and...

442
00:28:22.320 --> 00:28:23.360
Tauno.

443
00:28:25.040 --> 00:28:26.320
Tauno...

444
00:28:26.320 --> 00:28:28.880
You've said that
honesty is important.

445
00:28:28.920 --> 00:28:31.040
I'm just being honest with you.

446
00:28:31.960 --> 00:28:33.440
I'm just being honest.
